01:07:52.980 --> 01:07:54.860
Back to the Future was episode 212.

01:07:55.340 --> 01:07:56.800
That was the episode where I first got

01:07:56.800 --> 01:07:57.680
my new microphone,

01:07:57.680 --> 01:07:58.960
where everybody was like,

01:07:58.960 --> 01:08:00.700
oh, it's new mic, like he doesn't sound

01:08:00.700 --> 01:08:02.380
like he's talking out of a tin can.

01:08:02.600 --> 01:08:03.540
Some people were even like,

01:08:03.640 --> 01:08:05.100
oh, I missed the old mic.

01:08:06.360 --> 01:08:09.200
But this mic wasn't using his new mic

01:08:09.200 --> 01:08:11.140
when we recorded Back to the Future.

01:08:11.640 --> 01:08:15.360
And so I had to transcribe everything,

01:08:15.940 --> 01:08:18.100
re-record my lines on my own,

01:08:18.140 --> 01:08:20.220
and then insert them into the episode.

01:08:20.380 --> 01:08:21.360
And you didn't tell us.

01:08:21.460 --> 01:08:22.300
And I didn't tell you

01:08:22.300 --> 01:08:23.540
because I couldn't take that risk.

01:08:23.600 --> 01:08:24.600
I couldn't take that risk.

01:08:24.860 --> 01:08:26.640
And I was QC-ing the episode

01:08:26.640 --> 01:08:27.620
and I remember thinking like,

01:08:27.620 --> 01:08:29.160
something just sounds really weird.

01:08:29.340 --> 01:08:30.360
But I was like, whatever.

01:08:30.480 --> 01:08:31.300
It just sounds weird.

01:08:31.500 --> 01:08:33.100
And then you told us about it later,

01:08:33.360 --> 01:08:35.000
like months later.

01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:36.040
And I was like, oh my God,

01:08:36.120 --> 01:08:37.160
that makes so much sense now.

01:08:37.700 --> 01:08:39.360
Yep. So the Back to the Future episode

01:08:39.360 --> 01:08:43.040
was really me going back to the past

01:08:43.500 --> 01:08:46.040
to change the future of this podcast

01:08:46.040 --> 01:08:48.840
so that people know I have a good microphone.

01:08:49.500 --> 01:08:51.920
Well, I think that there was a period in time

01:08:52.480 --> 01:08:54.320
back when your mic was bad

01:08:54.320 --> 01:08:56.040
that I think that my,

01:08:56.200 --> 01:08:57.340
there was a moment

01:08:57.340 --> 01:08:59.640
where I had the best quality audio.

01:08:59.800 --> 01:09:01.120
And it was short-lived,

01:09:01.140 --> 01:09:02.800
but like, I don't know what happened.

01:09:02.940 --> 01:09:04.160
I'm still using the same mic.

01:09:04.320 --> 01:09:07.620
I'm surrounded by soft blankets and padding,

01:09:07.620 --> 01:09:09.400
but I sound horrible these days.

01:09:09.420 --> 01:09:11.120
I'm hoping this episode was like,

01:09:11.240 --> 01:09:13.340
was better than the last few episodes

01:09:13.340 --> 01:09:14.480
we've been having.

01:09:14.600 --> 01:09:16.200
But I cannot get myself to sound good.

01:09:16.200 --> 01:09:19.120
And since we're on a deep cuts train here,

01:09:19.340 --> 01:09:23.960
I will say that episodes 26 and 27 of season three,

01:09:24.220 --> 01:09:26.280
that is episodes 62 and 63,

01:09:26.820 --> 01:09:28.740
Lode Runner and Raid on Bungeling Bay,

01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:31.180
those two episodes are actually ones

01:09:31.180 --> 01:09:34.820
where the entire record got corrupted

01:09:34.820 --> 01:09:36.700
and we all had to rerecord,

01:09:36.780 --> 01:09:37.720
but we were all present.

01:09:37.900 --> 01:09:40.000
It wasn't like I took some of the old files

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:41.180
and some of the new files.

01:09:41.600 --> 01:09:43.960
That is just something that is kind of funny

01:09:43.960 --> 01:09:46.300
to think about that we pretended

01:09:46.300 --> 01:09:48.040
like we were doing them for the first time

01:09:48.040 --> 01:09:49.360
because it would just be embarrassing

01:09:49.360 --> 01:09:53.080
to acknowledge that we had to record twice.

01:09:53.380 --> 01:09:55.240
I think there were also at least two episodes

01:09:55.240 --> 01:09:56.620
where I was there,

01:09:56.640 --> 01:09:58.180
but my recording didn't work

01:09:58.180 --> 01:10:00.720
and you were able to just like work it

01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:03.860
so like you and Sean's audio was still there

01:10:03.860 --> 01:10:05.140
and you just cut out a few lines

01:10:05.140 --> 01:10:08.420
and like the whole episode was still like,

01:10:08.540 --> 01:10:09.680
I had been talking,

01:10:09.680 --> 01:10:11.160
but like it didn't record

01:10:11.160 --> 01:10:13.040
and we still made it sound like

01:10:13.040 --> 01:10:13.920
I just wasn't there.

01:10:14.240 --> 01:10:16.080
Yeah, hold on. I can get that episode as well.

01:10:16.500 --> 01:10:17.980
One of them might have been a Bites.

01:10:18.240 --> 01:10:20.140
Yeah, it was the Game Boy episode

01:10:20.960 --> 01:10:22.180
and Chess Master.

01:10:24.180 --> 01:10:25.740
That's pretty insane

01:10:25.740 --> 01:10:27.960
that we worked around

01:10:27.960 --> 01:10:30.160
a third of a conversation.

01:10:30.620 --> 01:10:32.200
Yeah, like go back and listen to it

01:10:32.200 --> 01:10:34.160
and see if there's anything that they were like responding to

01:10:34.160 --> 01:10:35.740
or you're like, wait, why are they saying that?

01:10:35.900 --> 01:10:37.140
Probably because it's something that I said.

01:10:37.300 --> 01:10:38.940
Definitely listen to the Chess Master episode

01:10:38.940 --> 01:10:39.820
because if I recall,

01:10:40.040 --> 01:10:42.580
Joe wasn't really that familiar with Chess

01:10:42.580 --> 01:10:45.740
and so you didn't say much to begin with,

01:10:45.760 --> 01:10:48.960
but I definitely didn't just like trim you out

01:10:48.960 --> 01:10:50.400
and trim out anytime we said Joe.

01:10:50.620 --> 01:10:52.880
I trimmed out like entire sections

01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:54.360
that just no longer worked

01:10:54.360 --> 01:10:56.160
because you said something meaningful.

01:10:56.440 --> 01:10:58.420
Yeah, but I feel like I actually might have been familiar

01:10:58.420 --> 01:10:59.640
with Chess at that point.

01:10:59.760 --> 01:11:00.960
No, no, you were. I'm joking.

01:11:01.380 --> 01:11:02.380
I'm saying that like-

01:11:02.380 --> 01:11:04.120
No, because I before, I just started,

01:11:04.120 --> 01:11:05.180
I just learned chess like,

01:11:05.200 --> 01:11:06.700
you know, very recently,

01:11:06.940 --> 01:11:08.420
relatively recently, but I was like,

01:11:08.520 --> 01:11:10.280
I don't know how I could have played Chess Master

01:11:10.280 --> 01:11:11.660
if I wasn't familiar with chess.

01:11:11.880 --> 01:11:12.980
Right, right. It would be impossible.

01:11:13.820 --> 01:11:16.000
All right. Sean, any secret episodes

01:11:16.000 --> 01:11:17.580
you want to tell the listeners about?

01:11:19.400 --> 01:11:21.520
No, I love hearing about these things

01:11:21.520 --> 01:11:24.960
because I just have zero memory for any of it.

01:11:25.380 --> 01:11:27.180
Yeah, actually this whole episode

01:11:27.180 --> 01:11:28.500
you've been talking about how

01:11:28.500 --> 01:11:30.100
people are going to think you have

01:11:30.100 --> 01:11:32.860
like short-term memory loss or something

01:11:32.860 --> 01:11:34.020
or long-term memory loss

01:11:34.020 --> 01:11:35.380
because this whole episode

01:11:35.380 --> 01:11:37.260
you've been saying that you don't remember anything.

01:11:39.020 --> 01:11:41.600
Well, I don't remember my childhood.

01:11:41.880 --> 01:11:45.000
I don't remember. I know who you guys are like in theory,

01:11:45.540 --> 01:11:47.300
but I don't remember like any like

01:11:47.300 --> 01:11:49.380
in-person conversations that we had.

01:11:49.520 --> 01:11:50.540
I don't know where we met.

01:11:50.860 --> 01:11:55.000
I don't know like where I am like now.

01:11:55.640 --> 01:11:57.880
Well, that's because you're actually not

01:11:57.880 --> 01:11:58.760
on this episode

01:11:58.760 --> 01:12:00.200
and we have just lifted bites

01:12:00.200 --> 01:12:01.680
